  "body": "**Stacked on #1640** - review only after da340c0f; merge #1615, #1622, #1634, #1640 first. (Fork synced at v0.18.0; branch based on #1640's head da340c0f.)\n\n## What changed\n\n#1621's neighbour law (`keep_law::neighbour_parts`) judged a part-source op against the setup's OTHER parts only when `depth_law_of` was not `None`. A Drill with cross holes reads `None` (its part law is the radial `cross_part`), so its neighbour set was empty, and the program sim does not judge a posed (radial) chain.\n\n- `keep_law::kept_models` now includes a part-source cross drill (`is_cross_drill`): the setup's parts but the source, fixtures and a stock-only model left out.\n- `cross_spindle::Solids` gains `neighbours`. After the source's own `cross_part::part_clear`, the new `cross_part::neighbours_clear` sweeps the finished chain (drill, shank, holder, rapids, posed along each move's axis) against those parts with **no hole wall excused**, on and off the work offset, and refuses by name.\n- A stock-source cross drill passes no neighbours (#1635 already judges every part in its stock).\n\n## Readings (reproduced first, on da340c0f)\n\nMill-turn bench, B = the #117 r10 punched bar with its r2 cross hole modelled (legal for B), A = a box; r20 bar and 40 x 40 box stocks, aligned and turned a quarter about Z; op on source \"B\".\n\n| case | before (all four stocks) | now |\n|---|---|---|\n| A x [12, 18] across the drill's line, no hole in A | generates clean, **posts** | refused: \"cross hole at (10, 0, 0) along (-1, 0, 0) cuts into a neighbouring part: another part the setup holds stands in the drill's line or its approach ...\"; nothing written |\n| A outside the raw bar, in the approach only | - | refused by name, aligned and turned |\n| A a tube whose r3 32-gon bore sits on the line (B's r3 hole at size) | - | refused (a neighbour's wall is never excused) |\n| A on B's far side, or 2 mm over the drill | posts | posts |\n\nSo it was a real P1: a gouge of part A posted unjudged on both stocks.\n\n## How tested\n\nPins in `crates/app/tests/cross_drill_neighbours.rs`:\n- `a_cross_drill_on_b_into_part_a_is_refused_by_name_on_both_stocks`\n- `a_cross_drill_whose_approach_crosses_part_a_is_refused_on_both_stocks`\n- `a_neighbours_round_hole_on_the_line_is_not_excused`\n- `a_cross_drill_on_b_clear_of_part_a_posts_on_both_stocks`\n- `over_mcp_a_part_source_cross_drill_answers_for_the_neighbour_the_same` (MCP parity: `add_operation` with `\"source\": \"B\"`)\n\nMutations (each alone, then reverted; `stock_source_cross_drill.rs` also run):\n\n| mutation | red |\n|---|---|\n| M1 cross drill out of `kept_models` (the old predicate) | into, approach, tube, MCP |\n| M2 `neighbours_clear` not called | into, approach, tube, MCP |\n| M3 source's hole walls excused on the neighbours | tube |\n| M4 2D tail's neighbour law skipped for a cross drill | none - so no guard was added; the tail's law stays on as a second net |\n| M5 part-source arm passes no neighbours | into, approach, tube, MCP |\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green on bf2dcaa7 (sim, motion, app, ui suites; 22.5 min, 0 failed); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA plain lathe holding two parts; the 3+2 frame arm (a cross drill is lathe / mill-turn work); MCP on a turned stock (`set_stock` takes no rotation).\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1641-cross-drill-neighbours.md`.\n\nChangelog: A part-source cross drill whose drill or approach enters another part in the setup is refused by name instead of posting (#1641)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1641\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
